{% layout none %}{%- comment -%}
  collection.cdc-json — JSON feed for the centre-diamond picker.

  New in v3, 31/08/2026. Ported from live's templates/collection.cdc-json.liquid
  (1,856 bytes), key for key, because the picker's client code filters and
  sorts on these exact names.

  ── HOW IT IS CALLED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NOT as /collections/loose-diamonds. Live moved off that in W029: Shopify
  silently stops applying storefront filters once a collection passes 5,000
  products, and Loose Diamonds holds 15,000+. So the picker asks the SHAPE
  SUB-COLLECTIONS instead, one request per origin:

      /collections/round-natural-diamonds?view=cdc-json&page=1
      /collections/round-lab-grown-diamonds?view=cdc-json&page=1

  Note the asymmetry in those handles — "natural" but "lab-grown". Carat
  travels as one filter.p.m.fye.carat param per 0.01ct step, because this
  store's metafield filters have no range operator and silently ignore
  trailing zeros (carat=0.30 returns nothing; carat=0.3 works). Repeated
  params OR correctly.

  This template is collection-agnostic on purpose: it renders whatever
  collection it is asked for, so the loose-diamonds URL still works as the
  fallback for a ring with no shape metafield.

  ── THINGS THAT WILL BREAK IT ─────────────────────────────────────────────

  · Sending an "Accept: application/json" header. Shopify content-negotiates
    /collections/... and returns the collection OBJECT json, ignoring ?view=.
    The fetch must send no Accept header.
  · Draft products never appear here, which is deliberate — a draft diamond is
    not for sale, and one in the picker is a stone we cannot deliver.
  · A trailing comma. The last-item guard below is load-bearing.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- paginate collection.products by 100 -%}
{
  "page": {{ paginate.current_page }},
  "pages": {{ paginate.pages }},
  "diamonds": [
    {%- for product in collection.products -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
        assign mf = product.metafields.fye

        comment
          First mp4 among the media, if any. The picker plays it on hover in
          place of the still, so a stone with a spin video sells itself.
        endcomment
        assign video_src = ''
        for m in product.media
          if m.media_type == 'video' and video_src == ''
            for src in m.sources
              if src.mime_type == 'video/mp4' and video_src == ''
                assign video_src = src.url
              endif
            endfor
          endif
        endfor
      -%}
    {
      "id": {{ product.id }},
      "variantId": {{ v.id }},
      "title": {{ product.title | json }},
      "price": {{ product.price | json }},
      "available": {{ product.available }},
      "sku": {{ v.sku | json }},
      "url": {{ product.url | json }},
      "image": {% if product.featured_image %}{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 480 | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
      "video": {{ video_src | json }},
      "shape": {{ mf.shape | json }},
      "carat": {{ mf.carat | json }},
      "colour": {{ mf.colour | json }},
      "clarity": {{ mf.clarity | json }},
      "certLab": {{ mf.cert_lab | json }},
      "certNumber": {{ mf.cert_number | json }},
      "origin": {{ mf.origin | json }}
    }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
{%- endpaginate -%}
